Compatibility renderer: don't make the mid-frame depth copy for SSAO.

With SSAO enabled, RasterizerSceneGLES3::_render_scene() flagged the frame as reading
the depth texture, which copies the (multisampled) depth + stencil buffer into the back
buffer before the transparent pass. SSAO never reads that copy: it runs in
_render_post_processing() on the internal depth buffer, which the MSAA resolve (or the
render itself, without MSAA) fills anyway. Only materials that sample DEPTH_TEXTURE need
the copy, and they still set used_depth_texture themselves in _fill_render_list().

On Windows browsers (ANGLE on Direct3D 11) resolving a multisampled stencil buffer goes
through a CPU readback, so the unused copy stalled every frame by about 3.4 ms on an
RTX 4080 (SSAO + 4x MSAA at 1080p: 7.2 ms of main-thread time per frame instead of 3.8).

--- a/drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp
+++ b/drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp
@@ -2701,11 +2701,6 @@
 	glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, fbo);
 	glViewport(0, 0, rb->internal_size.x, rb->internal_size.y);
 
-	// If SSAO is enabled, we definitely need the depth buffer.
-	if (ssao_enabled) {
-		scene_state.used_depth_texture = true;
-	}
-
 	// Do depth prepass if it's explicitly enabled
 	bool use_depth_prepass = config->use_depth_prepass;
 
